libpolycall provides CMake targets:

    find_package(libpolycall CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE libpolycall::libpolycall)

When consuming through vcpkg, configure your project with the vcpkg toolchain so
`find_package()` can discover `libpolycallConfig.cmake` automatically:

    cmake -S . -B build \
      -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=$VCPKG_ROOT/scripts/buildsystems/vcpkg.cmake

If you are not using the vcpkg toolchain, point CMake at the installed package prefix:

    cmake -S . -B build -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=<vcpkg_installed_triplet_prefix>

Optional features:

    "tools"  - builds and installs the `polycall` executable
    "tests"  - builds test executables during packaging
